.claude/worktrees/
# Rendered projection (derived from packages/mind/ideas via resolve.py; regenerable).
# A projection is NOT a deployment (projection-is-not-the-source): the render goes to a
# NEUTRAL staging dir that Claude Code does NOT auto-load -- deliberately NOT a
# `<repo>/.claude/{agents,skills}` tree, since a project-scoped session would load that
# AS a de-facto deployment merely because it was rendered. Scope is an accident applied
# at deploy time (deploy.py --scope ...), never a render side effect. The real deploy
# target is user-scope ~/.claude per host (C4); a `<repo>/.claude/{agents,skills}` tree
# may exist ONLY as an explicit `deploy.py --scope project` opt-in by a downstream adopter.
packages/mind/.render/
# The standalone TS projection (resolve.py's TS counterpart, src/toolkit/project-cli.ts).
# Same neutral-staging rationale as .render/ above; regenerable, never a deploy.
packages/mind/.render-ts/
# Fleet deploy topology carries env-specific SSH usernames — local-only.
# Committed template: .polis.config.example. Schema: docs/polis-config-schema.md
.polis.config
!.polis.config.example
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.scratchpad/
# Agent memory stores are per-agent home state — never repo-tracked (raw EPISODIC capture is agent-home only).
EPISODIC.jsonl
MEMORY.md
SELF.md
